  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A bond line structural formula is another method of structural representation of organic compounds. Here, every bond is represented as a line in a zigzag manner.  The carbon and hydrogen atoms are not written and do not appear in the structure. Only, the bonds present between the carbon atoms are shown.</p><p>In the bond-line formula for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HOCH</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>  is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d81d97c3-b0f3-479e-9353-75f3967c6feb.png\" style=\"width: 202px; height: 228px;\"/></p>",
